The receiver’s parameter T is called R in the method declaration. The method
declares its own T, which is a different parameter. Carry both R and T to the
generated function, using each in the input where it belongs.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Factory[T any] struct{}

//plumb:build
func (Factory[R]) Make[T any](value T) bool { return true }
